# Normalize every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux: the factory's gate and
# the VPS both check out on Linux, the owner's machine checks out with
# core.autocrlf=true. Without this line the same file is a different file on the
# two sides, and the failures that causes are the kind you cannot debug from the
# error message: `ruff format --check` reporting every file in the service as
# unformatted on one machine and none on the other, a shell script the host
# refuses to run with `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, a systemd unit that will not
# parse. Same command, different verdict, which is exactly the kind of gate you
# cannot trust.
#
# Git already stores LF in the object database, so this changes only what gets
# written to disk. Run `git add --renormalize .` after editing this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by the rule above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Force LF on shell scripts and Dockerfile. Redundant with the blanket rule
# above, and kept explicit because these are the files whose breakage is not
# cosmetic: deploy.sh, host-wrapper.sh and factory-stop.sh are run by the host,
# and a CRLF shebang line stops the deploy and the stop button.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# systemd unit files are parsed by systemd on the Linux host; CRLF causes
# "Failed to parse" at install time. deploy/ holds the deploy service, its
# timer and the failure-alert unit.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
